Implement FR-120, FR-121, and FR-122 for Quartermaster. Create `/home/cheta/code/quartermaster/src/core/guidance/render.ts`.

FR-120: Maintain canonical guidance file; translate to per-harness filename (CLAUDE.md for claude-code, AGENTS.md for codex/opencode/antigravity).
FR-121: Inject active pipeline directives into managed sections.
FR-122: Confine managed additions to clearly delimited sections, preserving developer content outside them.

Exact implementation:

```typescript
// Managed section delimiters
const MANAGED_START = (name: string) => `<!-- MANAGED BY QUARTERMASTER: ${name} -->`;
const MANAGED_END = '<!-- END MANAGED -->';
```

Export these functions:
```typescript
import type { GuidanceDocument, PipelineDefinition } from '@core/types';

interface GuidanceInput {
  canonical: string;
  pipelineDirectives: PipelineDefinition[];
  targetHarness: string;
  existingFile?: string;
}

export function renderGuidance(input: GuidanceInput): GuidanceDocument;
export function detectManagedSections(content: string): Array<{name: string; start: number; end: number; content: string}>;
export function harnessGuidanceFilename(harness: string): string; // returns 'CLAUDE.md' for 'claude-code', 'AGENTS.md' for others
```

Logic:
- `harnessGuidanceFilename`: 'claude-code' -> 'CLAUDE.md', everything else -> 'AGENTS.md'
- `detectManagedSections`: scan content line by line, find `<!-- MANAGED BY QUARTERMASTER: {name} -->` ... `<!-- END MANAGED -->` pairs. Return array with name, start/end char positions, content between delimiters. If opening tag without closing -> warn (console.warn), treat as unmanaged.
- `renderGuidance`:
  1. Start with `existingFile` content if provided, else empty string
  2. Remove all existing managed sections (replace with empty)
  3. Preserve all unmanaged content exactly
  4. Append canonical section: `<!-- MANAGED BY QUARTERMASTER: canonical -->\n{input.canonical}\n<!-- END MANAGED -->`
  5. For each pipeline in pipelineDirectives: append `<!-- MANAGED BY QUARTERMASTER: pipeline:{name} -->\n{directive content}\n<!-- END MANAGED -->`
  6. Return GuidanceDocument with path=filename, harness=targetHarness, managed=all managed content joined, unmanaged=preserved developer content, sections array

Import style: `import type { GuidanceDocument, PipelineDefinition } from '@core/types';`

Read `/home/cheta/code/quartermaster/src/core/types.ts` lines 230-246 first to see the GuidanceDocument type.

