Implement FR-060 and FR-061 for Quartermaster. Create `/home/cheta/code/quartermaster/src/core/deploy/status.ts`.

FR-060: Report for any harness which artifacts are currently deployed, by what method, and whether each matches its library source (in sync) or drifted.
FR-061: Detect and report orphaned deployments — files in target not in library.

The file should export:
```typescript
import { createHash } from 'crypto';
import { promises as fs } from 'fs';
import { join, basename } from 'path';
import type { Repository } from '@storage/repository';
import type { HarnessProfile, DeploymentRecord } from '@core/types';

export interface DeployedArtifact {
  artifactId: string;
  targetPath: string;
  method: 'link' | 'copy';
  inSync: boolean;
  libraryHash: string;
  deployedHash: string;
}

export interface HarnessStatus {
  harness: string;
  deployed: DeployedArtifact[];
  orphaned: string[];
  lastDeployment?: DeploymentRecord;
}

export async function getHarnessStatus(harness: string, repo: Repository, profile: HarnessProfile): Promise<HarnessStatus>;
```

Implementation:
- Load deployment records from repo.getDeployments(harness)
- For each operation in the most recent 'applied' record, check if target file exists and compute its SHA-256 hash vs the library source hash
- Walk harness target directories (all locations in profile.artifactTypes) to find files not accounted for by any deployment record — those are orphaned. Filter out .DS_Store, Thumbs.db, .gitkeep
- Use `createHash('sha256')` + file read for hash comparison
- Handle missing target dir gracefully (return empty status)

Import path style: `@core/types`, `@storage/repository` (these are tsconfig path aliases).

Use the existing code style from other files (see `/home/cheta/code/quartermaster/src/core/risk/scanner.ts` for pattern reference — it uses `import { promises as fs } from 'fs'` and `import { type Artifact, type RiskFlag } from '@core/types'`).

