Implement FR-140, FR-141, FR-142 for Quartermaster. Create TWO files:

1. `/home/cheta/code/quartermaster/src/core/safety/auditors.ts` (FR-140/141)
2. `/home/cheta/code/quartermaster/src/core/safety/findings.ts` (FR-142)

FR-140: Register external auditor tools, invoke them on artifacts, normalize findings.
FR-141: Gate deployment on configurable safety threshold; allow override with record.
FR-142: Trusted allowlist; extensible without code changes.

For `auditors.ts`, export:
```typescript
import type { Artifact, SafetyFinding, RiskSeverity } from '@core/types';

export interface AuditorConfig {
  name: string;
  command: string;      // command to run, {path} replaced with artifact path
  args?: string[];
  timeoutMs?: number;   // default 30000
  severityThreshold?: RiskSeverity;
  enabled: boolean;
}

export interface AuditorResult {
  auditor: string;
  passed: boolean;
  findings: SafetyFinding[];
  rawOutput?: string;
  durationMs: number;
  error?: string;
}

export interface SafetyReport {
  artifactId: string;
  auditors: AuditorResult[];
  passed: boolean;
  overridden?: boolean;
  overrideNote?: string;
}

export async function runAuditors(artifact: Artifact, configs: AuditorConfig[]): Promise<SafetyReport>;
export function thresholdGate(report: SafetyReport, threshold: RiskSeverity): boolean;
```

For `runAuditors`:
- For each enabled auditor config: spawn subprocess using `Bun.spawn` (or `child_process.spawn` as fallback) with artifact path substituted into command
- Capture stdout/stderr, parse as JSON if possible (look for `{findings: [...]}` shape), else treat rawOutput as one finding at 'low' severity
- Apply timeout: if process doesn't exit in timeoutMs, kill it and produce error finding at threshold severity
- If spawn fails (ENOENT): produce error finding at threshold severity with message 'auditor binary not found'
- Aggregate into SafetyReport. passed = no finding severity >= threshold (use SEVERITY_ORDER: low=0, medium=1, high=2, critical=3)

For `thresholdGate`: return true (passes) if no finding has severity >= threshold.

For `findings.ts`, export:
```typescript
export interface AllowlistEntry {
  kind: 'source' | 'artifact' | 'plugin';
  value: string;  // source URL pattern, artifact ID, or plugin name
  reason: string;
  addedAt: string;
}

export class AllowlistManager {
  constructor(private entries: AllowlistEntry[]) {}
  isAllowlisted(artifactId: string, sourceUrl?: string): boolean;
  add(entry: AllowlistEntry): void;
  remove(value: string): void;
  list(): AllowlistEntry[];
}

export function normalizeFinding(raw: unknown, auditorName: string, artifactId: string): SafetyFinding;
```

`normalizeFinding`: accepts raw parsed JSON object from auditor output, maps to SafetyFinding. If raw has `severity`, `description`, `recommendation` use them. Otherwise set severity='low', description=JSON.stringify(raw), recommendation='Review manually'.

Use import style: `import type { Artifact, SafetyFinding, RiskSeverity } from '@core/types';`

